--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acknowledgements — no code taken
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The adaptive trigger byte packing follows the format described by Nielk1's
TriggerEffectGenerator:

    https://gist.github.com/Nielk1/6d54cc2c00d2201ccb8c2720ad7538db

What was used is the wire format — which mode byte, which zone bits, where
the active-zone mask sits — which this library implements independently in C
and verifies against test vectors transcribed separately in Python. No source
was copied.

Report layouts, the CRC32 seed and the feature reports were worked out from
the Linux kernel's hid-playstation driver, the DS4Windows and pydualsense
projects, and public protocol notes, then checked against a real controller.
Where the sources disagreed, hardware decided. VERIFICATION.md records which
claim rests on which measurement.

